7. Predict the Output – Reverse Array
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
int main() {
int a[] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
for(int i = 0; i &lt; 5/2; i++) {
int temp = a[i];
a[i] = a[4-i];
a[4-i] = temp;
}
for(int i = 0; i &lt; 5; i++)
printf(&quot;%d &quot;, a[i]);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output.
Reverse Array
Initial:
1 2 3 4 5
Loop condition:
i < 5/2
Since 5/2 = 2 in integer division:
i = 0, 1
i = 0
Swap:
a[0] ↔ a[4]
Array becomes:
5 2 3 4 1
i = 1
Swap:
a[1] ↔ a[3]
Array becomes:
5 4 3 2 1
Output:
5 4 3 2 1
